INSERT INTO red_pill_verses (verse_id, claim_class, class_label, card_title, card_md, anchor_refs, tier_required, last_reviewed_at)
VALUES ((SELECT v.id FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON c.id = v.chapter_id JOIN books b ON b.id = c.book_id JOIN editions e ON e.id = b.edition_id WHERE e.slug = 'canon' AND b.slug = 'john' AND c.chapter_number = 20 AND v.verse_number = 28), 'direct', 'Spoken of him', 'My Lord and my Elohim (God)', $card$*And Thomas answered and said unto him, My Lord and my Elohim (God).* (John 20:28)

*I am Yahuah (LORD): that is my name: and my glory will I not give to another, neither my praise to graven images.* (Isaiah 42:8)

Thomas, a Torah-keeping son of Yashar'el (Israel), addresses the risen one to his face: *my Lord and my Elohim (God).* If the address were too high, this is the moment to refuse it — Yahuah (God) does not give his glory to another. Instead:

*Yahusha (Jesus) saith unto him, Thomas, because thou hast seen me, thou hast believed: blessed are they that have not seen, and yet have believed.* (John 20:29)

He receives the address and blesses everyone who will make it without seeing. The one who will not share his glory accepts this glory — because it is his.$card$, '{"Isaiah 42:8","John 20:29"}'::TEXT[], 'free', NOW())
